@startuml FRQ-MAIL-01-message-parser
' Viewpoint: one message from container to available data. Audience: analyst,
' implementer. A view, not a source of truth (D-13). Labels: UK English.
title FRQ-MAIL-01 — Reading a mail message

|A1 pass|
start
:Hand over a container;

|Reading|
if (Container belongs to this requirement?\n(by CONTENT, not by name — BR-04)) then (no)
  :Skip, record why;
  stop
else (yes)
endif

if (Carries a transport trace?) then (yes -- EV02)
  :Read the standard structure;
else (no -- EV03)
  if (External reader available?) then (no)
    :Fail BEFORE processing;
    stop
  else (yes)
  endif
  :Read what the client extracted;
endif

:Reduce headers to ONE named set\n(independent of the path taken);

|EV04 on demand|
fork
  :Parties — name + address,\nrepeats counted once (BR-02);
fork again
  :Times — instant + whether\nthe zone is KNOWN (BR-03);
fork again
  :Text — no executable content (BR-05);
fork again
  :Attachments — content + fingerprint;
  note right
    A broken attachment is dropped,
    the message continues (BR-06).
  end note
end fork

|Result|
:Same named data regardless\nof the container;
stop

note left
  Unreadable container: reported as a
  single failure class; the pass over the
  source location is not interrupted.
end note
@enduml
